Comment:
 The binary packages of this source tree also contain or link the following
 third-party components. They are not part of the GPL-3.0-only source files
 above and keep their own licenses:
 .
  * FFmpeg 8.1.2, linked statically into the release binaries. It is built
    with --enable-static --disable-shared and without --enable-gpl (and
    without --enable-nonfree), so the result is LGPL-2.1-or-later. The exact
    configure line is recorded in scripts/docker/Dockerfile.debian10 and
    scripts/docker/Dockerfile.rpm. Upstream source:
    https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.2.tar.xz
    (license text: https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html, LGPL v2.1 or later).
  * ONNX Runtime 1.21, linked statically into the official DEB/RPM/AppImage
    binaries (source builds may instead dlopen a system libonnxruntime, see
    debian/rules and CMakeLists.txt). License: MIT (see the
    "License: MIT" paragraph below). Source:
    https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/onnxruntime/ and
    https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
  * The ONNX Runtime C API header vendored under
    include/third_party/onnxruntime/ is MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft
    Corporation; see include/third_party/onnxruntime/LICENSE.

Files: resources/models/uvr-mdxnet-3-9662.onnx
Copyright: Ultimate Vocal Remover GUI (UVR) contributors (Anjok07, TRvlvr and contributors)
License: MIT
Comment:
 The vocal-removal model is distributed unmodified as a data asset; it is
 injected at build time via -DTER_MUSIC_BUNDLED_MODEL and installed as
 <prefix>/share/ter-music/models/uvr-mdxnet-3-9662.onnx together with
 models/NOTICE.md. The upstream release channel (TRvlvr/model_repo, GitHub
 Releases "all_public_uvr_models") ships no separate LICENSE file; the MIT
 terms below follow the UVR main project
 (https://github.com/Anjok07/ultimatevocalremovergui), which is MIT, and the
 model entry in its model_data.json. The file is not linked into the binary and
 remains under these MIT terms.

